  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116390",
      "title": "Enabling Routing & Adding a First Route",
      "lectureOrder": 268,
      "videoOrder": 256,
      "sourceHash": "e77249a6b5ecef3b715fd6a5b3661c5bc70ee49e81a8df027f1980d8cc464074",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.45,
          "end": 3.3,
          "en": "Now at the moment in this starting project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.3,
          "end": 6.93,
          "en": "I prepared for you, we have no routing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.93,
          "end": 8.64,
          "en": "We have the app component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.64,
          "end": 12.12,
          "en": "that's the component that's loaded and rendered initially,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.12,
          "end": 15.06,
          "en": "and it's then the components output in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.06,
          "end": 16.623,
          "en": "that we see on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.49,
          "end": 20.07,
          "en": "Now my idea here would be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.07,
          "end": 22.68,
          "en": "that we can, for example, select a user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.68,
          "end": 27.51,
          "en": "and as we do that, this part here of the UI should update,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.51,
          "end": 31.14,
          "en": "but I don't wanna do that by managing some state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.14,
          "end": 34.59,
          "en": "and by conditionally rendering some content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.59,
          "end": 38.76,
          "en": "But instead, I want to do that by loading a different URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.76,
          "end": 42.18,
          "en": "so that our address bar, address changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.18,
          "end": 46.65,
          "en": "and by then displaying different components on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.65,
          "end": 48.54,
          "en": "depending on the URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.54,
          "end": 51.603,
          "en": "because that's exactly what routing is all about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.68,
          "end": 54.33,
          "en": "And therefore, to make this work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.33,
          "end": 57.57,
          "en": "we need to add routing to this application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.57,
          "end": 61.98,
          "en": "We need to enable this Angular feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.98,
          "end": 65.88,
          "en": "And doing so is quite straightforward.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65.88,
          "end": 68.46000000000001,
          "en": "You need to go to your main.ts file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.46000000000001,
          "end": 70.98,
          "en": "and then provide a configuration object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.98,
          "end": 74.76,
          "en": "as a second argument for bootstrapApplication.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.76,
          "end": 76.44,
          "en": "In that second argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.44,
          "end": 79.68,
          "en": "you then need to configure your providers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.68,
          "end": 83.16,
          "en": "and call the provideRouter function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.16,
          "end": 87.18299999999999,
          "en": "which must be imported from at Angular router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 88.62,
          "end": 91.35,
          "en": "This will give you a router provider",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.35,
          "end": 94.47,
          "en": "configured and created by Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.47,
          "end": 96.36,
          "en": "and it's that router provider",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.36,
          "end": 100.35300000000001,
          "en": "that must be passed as a provider to that provider's array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.28,
          "end": 105.06,
          "en": "By the way, if you are using a module based application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105.06,
          "end": 107.94,
          "en": "where you're not calling bootstrapApplication,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 107.94,
          "end": 111.21000000000001,
          "en": "but where you instead have a root app module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 111.21000000000001,
          "end": 113.78999999999999,
          "en": "it works in essentially the same way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.78999999999999,
          "end": 116.22,
          "en": "There you would simply call provideRouter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.22,
          "end": 120.503,
          "en": "and pass the provider that gives you to the provider's array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 120.503,
          "end": 123.423,
          "en": "of your route module, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 124.35,
          "end": 127.05,
          "en": "Either way, provideRouter then wants",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 127.05,
          "end": 130.18,
          "en": "an array of routes as an argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 131.04,
          "end": 133.38,
          "en": "because you need to tell Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 133.38,
          "end": 137.73,
          "en": "which kind of routes you wanna support in your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 137.73,
          "end": 140.85,
          "en": "And a route in a nutshell in Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 140.85,
          "end": 145.62,
          "en": "is simply the combination of a path in your URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 145.62,
          "end": 149.57999999999998,
          "en": "and the information which component should become active",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 149.57999999999998,
          "end": 154.05,
          "en": "and should be loaded when that path becomes active.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 154.05,
          "end": 155.133,
          "en": "That's a route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 156.21,
          "end": 158.76,
          "en": "So a route is an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 158.76,
          "end": 160.75,
          "en": "where you define a path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 161.79,
          "end": 166.79,
          "en": "like tasks for your-domain slash tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 171.93,
          "end": 176.04,
          "en": "And then in addition to that path, the component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 176.04,
          "end": 177.81,
          "en": "The component that should be loaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 177.81,
          "end": 181.05,
          "en": "The component that should become active.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 181.05,
          "end": 184.53,
          "en": "Like for example, the TasksComponent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 184.53,
          "end": 188.82,
          "en": "which already exists in this project in the tasks folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 188.82,
          "end": 189.993,
          "en": "this component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 191.61,
          "end": 195.003,
          "en": "And which can therefore be imported and set as a component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 196.77,
          "end": 200.73,
          "en": "That's in a nutshell how you enable routing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 200.73,
          "end": 204.63,
          "en": "in your Angular application and how you register a route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 204.63,
          "end": 208.92000000000002,
          "en": "Though this setup here would not really be sufficient",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 208.92000000000002,
          "end": 211.98,
          "en": "for this application and will refine it soon",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 211.98,
          "end": 213.69,
          "en": "by adding more routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 213.69,
          "end": 216.03,
          "en": "But still, when it comes to enabling routing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 216.03,
          "end": 217.923,
          "en": "that is what you have to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 219.27,
          "end": 222.48,
          "en": "Now, since you typically have multiple routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 222.48,
          "end": 225.99,
          "en": "possibly up to dozens or hundreds of routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 225.99,
          "end": 229.29,
          "en": "in an Angular application, it is quite common",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 229.29,
          "end": 234.09,
          "en": "to outsource this route information and set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 234.09,
          "end": 236.763,
          "en": "and to store it in a different file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 237.87,
          "end": 239.85,
          "en": "So it is, for example, quite common",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 239.85,
          "end": 243.66,
          "en": "to create an app.routes.ts file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 243.66,
          "end": 245.733,
          "en": "next to your app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 247.89,
          "end": 250.743,
          "en": "And then you would grab your routes array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 251.67,
          "end": 255.27,
          "en": "cut that from the main.ts file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 255.27,
          "end": 258.69,
          "en": "and instead go to that app.routes.ts file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 258.69,
          "end": 261.76,
          "en": "And in there you would export a constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 262.74,
          "end": 267.69,
          "en": "called routes, for example, which must be of type routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 267.69,
          "end": 270.693,
          "en": "which is a type imported from Angular router,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 271.8,
          "end": 273.813,
          "en": "which holds that routes array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 274.8,
          "end": 278.25,
          "en": "And then of course you also must still import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 278.25,
          "end": 280.503,
          "en": "any component you are referencing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 283.26,
          "end": 287.46,
          "en": "With that outsourced, you could go back to the main.ts file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 287.46,
          "end": 290.97,
          "en": "and then reference your routes here by importing them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 290.97,
          "end": 292.82,
          "en": "and by passing them to provideRouter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 295.291,
          "end": 298.86,
          "en": "And if you wanted to, you could actually also grab",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 298.86,
          "end": 300.63,
          "en": "that configuration object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 300.63,
          "end": 304.26,
          "en": "and also cut that from the main.ts file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 304.26,
          "end": 307.92,
          "en": "And instead also add app.config.ts file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 307.92,
          "end": 310.35,
          "en": "next to app.routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 310.35,
          "end": 314.28,
          "en": "And there you could export an appConfig object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 314.28,
          "end": 317.4,
          "en": "which would be of type ApplicationConfig,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 317.4,
          "end": 319.953,
          "en": "which is also imported from Angular core,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 320.82,
          "end": 322.95,
          "en": "which is that configuration object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 322.95,
          "end": 325.593,
          "en": "we previously set up in the main.ts file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 326.82,
          "end": 330.42,
          "en": "And then here I would have to import provideRouter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 330.42,
          "end": 332.61,
          "en": "from at Angular router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 332.61,
          "end": 335.95,
          "en": "and import my routes from that app.routes file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 338.04,
          "end": 341.61,
          "en": "And then finally, in the main.ts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 341.61,
          "end": 346.61,
          "en": "we would import and use that app config thing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 348.75,
          "end": 351.783,
          "en": "and get rid of all the unused imports.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 352.86,
          "end": 357.09000000000003,
          "en": "That would give us a pretty lean and clean main.ts file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 357.09000000000003,
          "end": 359.31,
          "en": "Now this is all not required.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 359.31,
          "end": 360.99,
          "en": "These are just conventions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 360.99,
          "end": 364.5,
          "en": "so that you can keep your individual files lean and clean.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 364.5,
          "end": 367.32,
          "en": "But with that, we now do have routing enabled",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 367.32,
          "end": 369.09,
          "en": "for this application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 369.09,
          "end": 371.76,
          "en": "And therefore now it's time to add some more routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 371.76,
          "end": 373.593,
          "en": "to actually make this work.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
